# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global git ignores — linked to ~/.config/git/ignore, which is git's default
# excludes file ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore) when core.excludesFile is unset.
#
# This applies to EVERY repo on the machine, including other people's, so only
# patterns that are never a repo's real content belong here.
#
# commit.md is written by the global commit-log skill
# (configs/claude/.claude/skills/commit-log/SKILL.md): one proposed commit
# message for the current branch, scratch by definition. Ignoring it here
# keeps it out of every repo without editing anyone's .gitignore.
# Escape hatch, in a repo where the file is real content: git add -f commit.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
commit.md
